   # writing toward its own record.\n274-            if info.get(\"host\") != this_host:\n275-                age = invocation_age_s(info)\n276-                if age is not None and age < bound:\n277-                    in_flight.append(f\"{name} (host {info.get('host')} since {info.get('at')})\")\n278-                    continue\n279-            problems.append(f\"{name} started {info.get('at')} on {info.get('host')} \"\n280-                            f\"pid {info.get('pid')} and never wrote its record\")\n281-    if problems:\n282-        return p.fail(\"; \".join(problems), unrecorded_invocations=len(problems),\n283-                      running_invocations=running, in_flight=in_flight)\n284-    return p.hold(f\"{recorded} invocation(s) recorded, {len(running)} running, \"\n285-                  f\"{len(in_flight)} in flight elsewhere\",\n286-                  unrecorded_invocations=0, running_invocations=running, in_flight=in_flight)\n287-\n288-\n289-def proof_one_item_every_stage(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any] | None) -> Proof:\n290-    p = Proof(\"one-item-every-stage\", \"one item has traversed every stage\")\n291-    if m is None:\n292-        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\")\n293-    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n294-    records_dir = root / records_rel\n295-    items = load_records(records_dir)\n296-    if not items:\n297-        return p.fail(f\"no work item under {records_dir.relative_to(root)}\")\n298-    complete = [item for item, stages in items.items() if all(s in stages for s in STAGES)]\n299-    if not complete:\n300-        best = max(items.items(), key=lambda kv: len(kv[1]))\n301-        lacking = [s for s in STAGES if s not in best[1]]\n302-        return p.fail(f\"no item carries every stage; item {best[0]} lacks {', '.join(lacking)}\")\n303-\n304-    # issue #74: a complete item is counted only when its chain holds --\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-cppo0Ex7' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-w6Oul2mf' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n## Problem\n\nThe product cannot say what an item is waiting on. `attavo drive N` decides from the item's records and one read of the forge, and then either acts or prints one line into a log and exits: on #194 a concluded red check made it print \"stopped: forge checks not green\", exit 1, and write nothing, twice, while the operator screen showed a Launch button (#171). The decision is already a pure function (`drive_state` plus `read_forge_checks`); nothing exposes it without also acting on it, so every view derives its own answer and a refusal is an event nobody recorded instead of a level anybody can read.\n\nThis is R1 of the reconciler (`claude/reconciler-brief-2026-09-20.md`, rulings A and G, 2026-09-20): `attavo drive N --report` prints, as JSON against `schema/drive-report.schema.json`, the item's state, whose move it is (`yours`, `waits`, `acts`, `done`), and one sentence in the operator's words. It writes nothing, starts nothing, and never waits: it reads the forge once and does not call `poll_forge_checks`. No behaviour of `attavo drive N` without the flag changes. The states are the ones today's product can be in; attempt budgets, the breaker, and rulings arrive with R3 and R4 and add states then.\n\nThe stub under `stub/` is thin on purpose (the operator's ruling, 2026-09-20): it guesses the state from which files exist, satisfies the criteria, and fails eight of the thirteen tests in `tests/test_report.py`, which cover what it ignores (an expired approval, a record bound to an earlier approval or build, a live invocation inside and past the bound, counsel, a merged item). The build writes the report from the product's own functions; shipping the stub's `report.py` is not a build.\n\nThe build's own gate (`[checks].command`) does not run the type check that CI requires, so a build can pass here and leave the head red: `build-01` did, on one `return-value` error at `attavo/report.py` line 57 (`_counsel_of` returns a `CounselRecord` where its annotation says `dict[str, Any]`). `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the built tree, with no `type: ignore`; the builder runs it before it finishes.\n\nA new reader must not wedge on a record that already exists (#194's `verify-01`): the report returns a state for every item this repository's records directory carries.\n\nRetires: #171 (a refusal is the report's current level, recomputed on every read, so there is nothing to record); any view's own derivation of what an item is waiting on (deleted by a screen item filed against this one once a release carries it).\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/report.py\n- attavo/drive.py\n- attavo/types.py\n- attavo/cli.py\n- schema/drive-report.schema.json\n- tests/test_report.py\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n- tests/test_cli_help.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh: with a built item whose head carries a concluded red check, drive 1 --report exits 0, prints state blocked-on-checks, kind waits, stage verify, the check by name and conclusion, and a sentence naming the check and the head that says neither \"drive\" nor \"verify\"; HEAD, the working tree, and the item's records directory are the same before and after\n- report-never-waits.sh: with a check still in_progress and the drive's poll bound set to 30 s, the report returns in under 10 s with state waiting-on-checks and the check named\n- report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh: across one item's life the report reads waiting-on-approval yours, next-build acts, owes-recovery acts naming build attempt 1 as died (and writes no record), stopped yours naming build-01, its class, and its filed issue, next-review acts, and ready-to-merge yours\n- the-report-has-its-contract-and-its-tests.sh: schema/drive-report.schema.json closes its properties, requires every one, and enumerates the eleven states and four kinds; DriveReport mirrors it in tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py; tests/test_report.py carries its thirteen tests by name\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-JEl95Gxz' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-bkgON4rC' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n{\n  \"sha\": \"3c9fe604d61798f2f2a78fe220700ea1d363b681\",\n  \"spec_sha\": \"3c9fe604d61798f2f2a78fe220700ea1d363b681\",\n  \"at\": \"2026-09-20T18:01:01Z\",\n  \"status\": \"built\",\n  \"approval_sha\": null,\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh\",\n      \"on_tree\": 0,\n      \"on_stub\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"report-never-waits.sh\",\n      \"on_tree\": 0,\n      \"on_stub\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh\",\n      \"on_tree\": 0,\n      \"on_stub\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"the-report-has-its-contract-and-its-tests.sh\",\n      \"on_tree\": 0,\n      \"on_stub\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"refusal\": null,\n  \"record_version\": 2,\n  \"item\": \"206\",\n  \"product_version\": \"v0.26.0\",\n  \"product_pin\": \"v0.26.0\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '80,155p' attavo/drive.py && sed -n '60,125p' attavo/doctor.py && sed -n '1,110p' attavo/doctor.py && rg -n 'drive .*--report|--report' tests attest/specs/206/criteria | head -100 && git diff 3c9fe604d61798f2f2a78fe220700ea1d363b681 8c85d4291bab1bcf3bb31d6be0a877789eb0f195 -- attest/specs/206/spec.md attest/records/206/spec-03.json && git diff 8c85d4291bab1bcf3bb31d6be0a877789eb0f195 0e8ab9c37017f066e677379c74a31ad29b5280e3 -- attavo/report.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '80,155p' attavo/drive.py && sed -n '60,125p' attavo/doctor.py && sed -n '1,110p' attavo/doctor.py && rg -n 'drive .*--report|--report' tests attest/specs/206/criteria | head -100 && git diff 3c9fe604d61798f2f2a78fe220700ea1d363b681 8c85d4291bab1bcf3bb31d6be0a877789eb0f195 -- attest/specs/206/spec.md attest/records/206/spec-03.json && git diff 8c85d4291bab1bcf3bb31d6be0a877789eb0f195 0e8ab9c37017f066e677379c74a31ad29b5280e3 -- attavo/report.py\"","aggregated_output":"        run = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"push\", \"origin\", f\"HEAD:{branch}\"],\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n        return run.returncode == 0, run.stderr.strip()\n\n    ok, err = attempt()\n    if ok:\n        return True, None\n    pull = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"pull\", \"--no-rebase\", \"--no-edit\",\n                           \"origin\", branch], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if pull.returncode != 0:\n        return False, f\"push rejected and the retry merge failed: {pull.stderr.strip() or err}\"\n    ok, err = attempt()\n    if not ok:\n        return False, f\"push rejected again after merging {branch}: {err}\"\n    return True, None\n\n\ndef drive_state(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], item_id: str) -> tuple[str, str | None, Path]:\n    \"\"\"(\"no-approval\" | \"build\" | \"verify\" | \"ready\", detail, records_dir):\n    the next mechanical step for item_id, read from its latest records\n    alone. A build only counts as current when it is a pass bound to the\n    valid approval's own sha; a verify only counts as current when it is a\n    pass bound to that build's own sha -- the same staleness a re-approval\n    or a re-build must force, attest's own chain check already enforces\n    (check_attest_chain), read here rather than re-typed.\"\"\"\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    status = approval_status(root, m, item_id)\n    if status != \"valid\":\n        return \"no-approval\", status, records_dir\n\n    latest_approval = latest_record(records_dir, \"approval\")\n    latest_build = latest_record(records_dir, \"build\")\n    build_current = (latest_build is not None and latest_build.get(\"status\") == \"pass\"\n                     and latest_build.get(\"approval_sha\")\n                     == (latest_approval.get(\"sha\") if latest_approval else None))\n    if latest_build is None or not build_current:\n        return \"build\", None, records_dir\n\n    latest_verify = latest_record(records_dir, \"verify\")\n    verify_current = (latest_verify is not None and latest_verify.get(\"status\") == \"pass\"\n                      and latest_verify.get(\"build_sha\") == latest_build.get(\"sha\"))\n    if not verify_current:\n        return \"verify\", None, records_dir\n\n    return \"ready\", None, records_dir\n\n\ndef _drive_run_stage(root: Path, records_dir: Path, branch: str, stage: str,\n                      item_id: str) -> tuple[int, bool]:\n    \"\"\"Runs build or verify in-process -- the same command `attavo build`\n    or `attavo verify` would run, printing the same reason on a refusal,\n    failure, or halt -- and returns (rc, done): done is False only when\n    the record just written carries status \"pass\" (a stage command's own\n    exit code says nothing about that: cmd_verify exits 0 on a \"returned\"\n    record too, since returning is not an operational error). A non-pass\n    record is counseled (cmd_counsel, issue #100) and filed (cmd_file_stops,\n    issue #89) before it is transported,\n    so a stop's own counsel record and .filed marker -- the filing\n    command's stdout, the issue file-stops just opened -- exist on disk\n    in time to be committed and pushed in the very same commit as the\n    stage record and its log; a marker written only after the push would\n    never reach the ledger at all, and a second worktree or a fresh clone\n    would refile every stop it finds with no marker beside it. The stage\n    record and the counsel record (when one was written) are then\n    transported together: committed with commit_record and pushed with\n    push_record_commit, whatever the stage record's status -- the record\n    pushes stay the same pushes, made by drive in the run that produced\n    the record (issue #84's rule 42 row).\"\"\"\n    before = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, stage)\n\n    # The invocation's marker, committed and pushed before the stage runs:\n    # one commit per attempt, so that an invocation which dies or hangs\n    # is a fact on the branch (proof five) and not a silence.\n    nn = next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage)\n\n\ndef _merges_reachable(root: Path) -> tuple[list[dict[str, Any]], str | None]:\n    \"\"\"(merges, refusal): every merge commit on the default branch's own\n    first-parent line -- sha, parents, and its own first-parent diff --\n    read by one process rather than the git log plus one git diff per\n    merge merge_introducing_records used to pay walking toward the one\n    it wants (issue #153). refs/remotes/origin/HEAD names the default\n    branch without hard-coding \"main\", the same primitive\n    diff_since_approval already uses (issue #52); walking from it rather\n    than from HEAD is what keeps a transport merge on an item branch, a\n    pull_request checkout's own synthetic test merge, and a merge_group's\n    temporary merge from ever being mistaken for an item's merge (issue\n    #169) -- none of those is reachable from the default branch's first-\n    parent line by definition. When refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set,\n    this refuses by name rather than guess, exactly as diff_since_approval\n    does.\n\n    The walk starts at HEAD itself when the current checkout is literally\n    on the branch refs/remotes/origin/HEAD names (an ordinary checkout of\n    the default branch, on push or on a developer's own machine) and at\n    the remote-tracking ref's own value otherwise (any other branch, or\n    the detached HEAD a pull_request or merge_group checkout leaves\n    behind) -- HEAD only ever *is* the default branch's first-parent line\n    in the former case; in the latter, only the remote-tracking ref names\n    it. --diff-merges=first-parent gives each merge's diff against its\n    first parent in the same pass git log --merges already makes to list\n    them, in the same order, newest first.\"\"\"\n    symref = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if symref.returncode != 0:\n        return [], \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set; run `git remote set-head origin -a`\"\n    default_remote_ref = symref.stdout.strip()\n    default_branch = default_remote_ref.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1]\n    current_branch = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    default_ref = (\"HEAD\" if current_branch.returncode == 0\n                   and current_branch.stdout.strip() == default_branch\n                   else default_remote_ref)\n    try:\n        out = git(root, \"log\", default_ref, \"--first-parent\", \"--merges\",\n                 \"--diff-merges=first-parent\", \"--name-only\",\n                 \"--format=\\x01%H\\x1f%P\")\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return [], None\n    merges = []\n    for block in out.split(\"\\x01\")[1:]:\n        header, _, rest = block.partition(\"\\n\")\n        sha, parents = header.split(\"\\x1f\")\n        merges.append({\"sha\": sha, \"parents\": parents.split(),\n                       \"touched\": [line for line in rest.splitlines() if line.strip()]})\n    return merges, None\n\n\ndef merge_introducing_records(root: Path, records_rel: str, item: str,\n                              stages: tuple[str, ...],\n                              merges: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"(merge_sha, refusal): the merge commit on the default branch's own\n    first-parent line whose first-parent diff introduces a record for\n    every one of stages, under records_rel/item/ -- the same derivation\n    attest itself uses (derive_attest_items), read here so proof two\n    requires an item's stage records to have arrived by an actual merge\n    on the default branch, not merely to sit in the tree, and not by a\n    transport merge, a pull_request checkout's synthetic test merge, or a\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport fnmatch\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom attavo.attest import check_attest_chain, item_time_and_cost\nfrom attavo.common import (\n    MANIFEST,\n    Proof,\n    STAGES,\n    fixture_item_id,\n    git,\n    product_version,\n    read_manifest,\n)\nfrom attavo.records import RECORD_RE, load_records, parse_attempts\nfrom attavo.stops import STOP_CLASSES, STOP_PROVENANCES, STOP_STAGES, gate_stop\n\n# --- doctor's three proofs ---\n\ndef proof_every_gate_rejects(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any] | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"every-gate-rejects\", \"every gate rejects its fixture\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no gate is registered\")\n    gates = m.get(\"gates\") or {}\n    if not gates:\n        return p.fail(\"[gates] is empty; a gate that has rejected nothing does not exist\")\n    fixtures = root / m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"rejections\", \"\")\n    # Proposal, not yet ruled on (issue #54): a gate that retires nothing\n    # only adds, so proof one reports it here rather than waiting on the\n    # schema alone -- read_manifest never validates against the manifest\n    # schema at runtime, so a schema requirement is not an enforced one.\n    no_retires = [name for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()) if not gate.get(\"retires\")]\n    missing, accepted = [], []\n    for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()):\n        fixture = fixtures / name\n        if not fixture.is_dir():\n            missing.append(name)\n            continue\n        env = dict(os.environ)\n        item = fixture_item_id(fixture)\n        if item is not None:\n            env[\"ATTAVO_ITEM\"] = item\n        run = subprocess.run(gate[\"command\"], shell=True, cwd=str(fixture),\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\n        if run.returncode == 0:\n            accepted.append(name)\n    if missing:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) with no rejection fixture: {', '.join(missing)}\")\n    if accepted:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) that accepted their rejection fixture: {', '.join(accepted)}\")\n    if no_retires:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) with no retires: {', '.join(no_retires)}\")\n    return p.hold(f\"{len(gates)} gate(s) rejected their fixture\")\n\n\ndef _merges_reachable(root: Path) -> tuple[list[dict[str, Any]], str | None]:\n    \"\"\"(merges, refusal): every merge commit on the default branch's own\n    first-parent line -- sha, parents, and its own first-parent diff --\n    read by one process rather than the git log plus one git diff per\n    merge merge_introducing_records used to pay walking toward the one\n    it wants (issue #153). refs/remotes/origin/HEAD names the default\n    branch without hard-coding \"main\", the same primitive\n    diff_since_approval already uses (issue #52); walking from it rather\n    than from HEAD is what keeps a transport merge on an item branch, a\n    pull_request checkout's own synthetic test merge, and a merge_group's\n    temporary merge from ever being mistaken for an item's merge (issue\n    #169) -- none of those is reachable from the default branch's first-\n    parent line by definition. When refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set,\n    this refuses by name rather than guess, exactly as diff_since_approval\n    does.\n\n    The walk starts at HEAD itself when the current checkout is literally\n    on the branch refs/remotes/origin/HEAD names (an ordinary checkout of\n    the default branch, on push or on a developer's own machine) and at\n    the remote-tracking ref's own value otherwise (any other branch, or\n    the detached HEAD a pull_request or merge_group checkout leaves\n    behind) -- HEAD only ever *is* the default branch's first-parent line\n    in the former case; in the latter, only the remote-tracking ref names\n    it. --diff-merges=first-parent gives each merge's diff against its\n    first parent in the same pass git log --merges already makes to list\n    them, in the same order, newest first.\"\"\"\n    symref = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if symref.returncode != 0:\n        return [], \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set; run `git remote set-head origin -a`\"\n    default_remote_ref = symref.stdout.strip()\n    default_branch = default_remote_ref.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1]\n    current_branch = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    default_ref = (\"HEAD\" if current_branch.returncode == 0\n                   and current_branch.stdout.strip() == default_branch\n                   else default_remote_ref)\n    try:\n        out = git(root, \"log\", default_ref, \"--first-parent\", \"--merges\",\n                 \"--diff-merges=first-parent\", \"--name-only\",\n                 \"--format=\\x01%H\\x1f%P\")\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return [], None\n    merges = []\n    for block in out.split(\"\\x01\")[1:]:\n        header, _, rest = block.partition(\"\\n\")\n        sha, parents = header.split(\"\\x1f\")\nattest/specs/206/criteria/report-never-waits.sh:26:$A drive 1 --report > \"$tmp/report.json\"\nattest/specs/206/criteria/report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh:26:$A drive 1 --report > \"$tmp/report.json\"\nattest/specs/206/criteria/report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh:22:state() { $A drive 1 --report | python3 -c 'import json,sys; r=json.load(sys.stdin); print(r[\"state\"], r[\"kind\"])'; }\nattest/specs/206/criteria/report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh:38:$A drive 1 --report > \"$tmp/owes.json\"\nattest/specs/206/criteria/report-walks-an-item-and-names-whose-move-it-is.sh:49:$A drive 1 --report > \"$tmp/stopped.json\"\ntests/test_report.py:1:\"\"\"`attavo drive N --report`: what one item is waiting on and for whom, as a\ntests/test_report.py:42:    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", item, \"--report\", env=env)\ntests/test_report.py:226:    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", \"--report\")\ntests/test_cli_help.py:40:    assert \"attavo drive [N] [--until-ready | --report]\" in run.stdout\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-oyvzzNxj' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-AP9O8TWJ' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ndiff --git a/attest/records/206/spec-03.json b/attest/records/206/spec-03.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..54f6f85\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/attest/records/206/spec-03.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+{\n+  \"sha\": \"3c9fe604d61798f2f2a78fe220700ea1d363b681\",\n+  \"spec_sha\": \"3c9fe604d61798f2f2a78fe220700ea1d363b681\",\n+  \"at\": \"2026-09-20T18:01:01Z\",\n+  \"status\": \"built\",\n+  \"approval_sha\": null,\n+  \"criteria\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"report-names-a-red-check-and-writes-nothing.sh\",\n+      \"